  "text": "כלול\n\n目的是\n\nᴊ */\n.Project\n∠Always1\nנותן\nשיעייא\n主题教育区\n犹 しておく\n的角度\n thù roup\n{}{\nイベAttend\naddComponent\nクトิ\n_coordinates:\n${data\n_{mk_activities\n_记\nroots_\nlte进食憩\n_J\nuntime\n•\n• 분아\nendentifeī•\nTo find the locus of the centers \\((a,b)\\) of all circles that intersect the parabola \\( y^2 = 4x \\) at two distinct points such that the line segment connecting these points is perpendicular to the tangent line to the parabola at its midpoint, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Parabola Properties and Tangent Line Equation:**\n   - The parabola is \\( y^2 = 4x \\).\n   - The midpoint of the line segment connecting the two points of intersection with the parabola lies on the vertical line passing through the focus of the parabola.\n   - The focus of the parabola is at \\( (1,0) \\).\n\n2. **Tangent Line Equation:**\n   - The tangent line to the parabola at a point \\((t^2/4, t)\\) has the equation:\n     \\[\n     y = \\frac{t}{2} x - \\frac{t^3}{8}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Intersection Points:**\n   - Let the points of intersection be \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\).\n   - These points satisfy the parabola equation \\( y^2 = 4x \\) and the line equation \\( y = \\frac{t}{2} x - \\frac{t^3}{8} \\).\n\n4. **Perpendicular Line Condition:**\n   - The line segment connecting \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) is perpendicular to the tangent line at the midpoint \\((m, m)\\) of these points.\n   - The slope of the tangent line at the midpoint is \\( \\frac{t}{2} \\), so the slope of the perpendicular line is \\( -2/t \\).\n\n5. **Midpoint Calculation:**\n   - The midpoint \\((m, m)\\) is given by:\n     \\[\n     m = \\frac{x_1 + x_2}{2} = \\frac{t^2}{16}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     m = \\frac{y_1 + y_2}{2} = \\frac{t}{16}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Circle Equation:**\n   - The circle with center \\((a, b)\\) passing through the points \\((x_1, y_1)\\) and \\((x_2, y_2)\\) has the equation:\n     \\[\n     (x - a)^2 + (y - b)^2 = (x_1 - a)^2 + (y_1 - b)^2 = (x_2 - a)^2 + (y_2 - b)^2\n     \\]\n\n7. **Intersection with Parabola and Line:**\n   - Substitute the parametric form of the points into the circle equation and the parabola equation.\n\n8. **Solving for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\):**\n   - Using the conditions derived from the midpoint and the perpendicularity, solve for \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) in terms of \\(t\\).\n\n9. **Eliminat teh Coefficients:**\n   - Combine the equations to eliminate \\(t\\) and find the locus in the form \\(Pa^2 + Qb^2 + Ra + Sb + T = 0\\).\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-8a^2 + b^2 - 4a + 8b - 4 = 0}\n\\]",
